error: value sent on `ep.res` does not live long enough
  --> should_fail/send-value-expired.anvil:12:9
   |
12 |         send ep.res (inc_x) >>
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the value is sent here and must stay valid until 1 cycle after it is sent
  --> should_fail/send-value-expired.anvil:9:17
   |
 9 |         let x = recv ep.req >>
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^ the value depends on this `recv ep.req` and is only valid until 1 cycle after it
   = help: store the value in a register while it is still valid (`set r := ...`) and send `*r` instead
   = help: alternatively, declare a longer lifetime for `req` in channel class `ch`; it is `@#1` now

